# Spatial Drones - Vision Document

## Project Purpose

3D spatial mapping system using WiFi signal propagation patterns from
mesh-connected drone chains. Each node in the chain acts as a radar-like
sensor, measuring signal reflections and strengths to build a volumetric
model of the explored space.

## Core Philosophy

Most of the world is fine. We just don't have good maps of it.

Civilians generating complete mappings of their spaces - homes, towns,
nations - reveals that anomalies are rare. The monotony is worth celebrating.
When we can see that infrastructure works, that buildings stand, that roads
connect, we stop imagining threats in every shadow.

## Key Components

1. Signal Analysis Module - WiFi RSSI, time-of-flight, multipath analysis
2. Drone Chain Protocol - Relay chains extending mapping range
3. Voxel Map System - 3D volumetric representation
4. Export Formats - PLY, OBJ, GeoJSON for external tools

## Applications

- Building inspection
- Search and rescue
- Infrastructure audit
- Archaeological survey
- Community mapping projects

